# TODO

## Interactive headless controller

The `headless-opengl` backend exposes queued keyboard, mouse, touch, scroll,
and system-action input through `HeadlessOpenGLApp.Controller`. It runs on a
Mesa surfaceless EGL pbuffer with llvmpipe and advances only when its owner
calls `step`.

Add a controller process that streams captured frames and accepts input without
linking the controller transport into game code. A browser client is the likely
first frontend. Keep the transport protocol useful for both people and AI
agents.

The runner also needs an injectable clock for code that does not use the frame
delta, deterministic scheduler and asset-completion controls, and a Bazel test
helper that stores failed frame captures as test artifacts.
